# ckit shared runtime state and recoverable sidecars
# CONTINUITY.md is the live working-memory scratchpad: high-churn by design,
# rewritten every turn, and meaningful only on the machine that wrote it.
# claude-kit's own rule (.claude/rules/continuity.md) says never commit it --
# it was tracked here by accident and touched 12 commits on this branch alone.
# The committed counterpart is .ckit/agent-memory/, which is durable and low-churn.
.ckit/CONTINUITY.md
.ckit/state/*
!.ckit/state/.gitkeep
.ckit/tmp/*
!.ckit/tmp/.gitkeep
.ckit/config/upgrade-in-progress.json
.ckit.bak-*/
.claude.bak-*/
.codex.bak-*/
.agents.bak-*/
.claude-kit-txn-*/
.claude-kit-managed-execution.lock
*.claude-kit
*.codex-kit

# ui-kit build products and deps
ui-kit/node_modules/
ui-kit/dist/
# design-sync: the durable inputs (config.json, NOTES.md, conventions.md,
# previews/, overrides/) ARE committed so a re-sync on another machine
# reuses them. Only machine state and staged scripts are ignored.
.design-sync/.cache/
.design-sync/learnings/
.design-sync/node_modules/
ds-bundle/
.ds-sync/
